  "comment": "The eight step latches of the upper sequencer share one line and the sixteen of the lower share another: within a sequencer they differ only by step number. The CV Steps and CV Reverse inputs write their result back into the panel parameter every sample, so those two switches cannot be moved by hand while a cable is toggling them faster than you can click. The clock input is a level compare at 1V feeding a Schmitt trigger on the resulting boolean, so an input that never falls below 1V never clocks again. Nothing in this plugin saves module state to the patch; only parameter positions come back. Every jack is read with getVoltage(), so nothing is polyphonic."
